  "prompt": "Is a new business required to register with the BIR, and what form is used?",
  "runtimeCommit": "b7e40fc2af25db1c9eebbb23d1d537b3ec4bf1c8",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, a new business is required to register with the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) before commencing operations. The registration must be done using BIR Form No. 1901 for self-employed individuals or BIR Form No. 1902 for employees earning compensation income.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor new businesses, timely registration with the BIR is crucial to avoid penalties and ensure compliance with tax laws. Completing the appropriate registration form allows the business to obtain a Tax Identification Number (TIN), which is necessary for tax filings and transactions. Failure to register can lead to complications in tax compliance and potential legal issues.",
